        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Intermittent episodes of heart racing"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Episodes occur 1–2 times per week, with sudden onset, peak over a few minutes, and last approximately 5–10 minutes. Often occur in the evenings when alone or when thinking about health or an article about pregnant women and panic. Can occur at rest; no clear exertional link."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
